{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789314379,"nonce":"Nn/Ua7NNa9V2jroQNJ41rd1cHZg=","title":"Snapshot: an HIR snapshot the host cannot use must fail loudly","message":"`Snapshot::module()` attaches the prelowered HIR only when `usable_here()` holds (same `BUILD_ID`, same pointer size). When it does not, the module's declarations come back body-stripped by `SnapshotBuilder::module_lowered` and cannot be lowered again: the frontend gets declarations with no bodies and links nothing, or worse, lowers externs for every library function and fails at run time with unresolved symbols.\n\nDecision: refuse, with an error naming the mismatch (build id or pointer width), rather than degrade. A frontend that wants to fall back parses its library source instead; the Python crate ships the source too, so `build.rs` can make that fallback explicit.\n\nNot yet implemented; noted while landing the ZSNAP v4 HIR snapshot.","files":null}]}